# B01: Fixed-Capacity Ring Buffer (`RingBuffer`)

This module provides a zero-heap-allocation, fixed-capacity (`8` `i32` elements) circular queue `RingBuffer`, designed for embedded sensor sampling windows, audio frame buffering, and high-throughput message queues.

## Core Design Constraints
1. **Zero Dynamic Allocation**: Uses an inline fixed-size array `[8]i32` with modulo wrap-around read/write indices.
2. **Structural Invariants (`invariant`)**: Current element count `len` never exceeds `capacity` (`8`), and both `head` and `tail` indices remain strictly within `[0, capacity)`.
3. **First-Class Contract Guards**:
   - Before `push`, if the buffer is full, the precondition `requires ... else RingError.Full` intercepts the call with a deterministic error; on success, `ensures` guarantees `self.len == old(self.len) + 1`.
   - Before `pop`, if the buffer is empty, `requires ... else RingError.Empty` intercepts the call; on success, `ensures` guarantees `self.len == old(self.len) - 1`.

```jenny
module ring_buffer

pub enum RingError {
    Full,
    Empty,
}

pub struct RingBuffer {
    pub data: [8]i32,
    pub head: usize = 0,
    pub tail: usize = 0,
    pub len: usize = 0,
    pub capacity: usize = 8,

    invariant {
        self.capacity == 8
        self.len <= self.capacity
        self.head < self.capacity
        self.tail < self.capacity
    }
}

impl RingBuffer {
    pub fn new() -> RingBuffer
        ensures result.len == 0
        ensures result.capacity == 8

    pub fn is_empty(self) -> bool
        ensures result == (self.len == 0)

    pub fn is_full(self) -> bool
        ensures result == (self.len == self.capacity)

    pub fn push(mut self, val: i32) -> void ! RingError
        requires self.len < self.capacity else RingError.Full
        ensures self.len == old(self.len) + 1

    pub fn pop(mut self) -> i32 ! RingError
        requires self.len > 0 else RingError.Empty
        ensures self.len == old(self.len) - 1

    pub fn peek(self) -> i32 ! RingError
        requires self.len > 0 else RingError.Empty
        ensures self.len == old(self.len)
}

@example("EX-B01-01: normal push, peek, pop and wrap-around") {
    var rb = RingBuffer.new()
    assert(rb.is_empty())

    rb.push(10)!
    rb.push(20)!
    rb.push(30)!
    assert(rb.len == 3)
    assert(rb.peek()! == 10)

    val first = rb.pop()!
    assert(first == 10)
    assert(rb.len == 2)

    val second = rb.pop()!
    val third = rb.pop()!
    assert(second == 20)
    assert(third == 30)
    assert(rb.is_empty())
}

@example("EX-B01-02: boundary conditions Full and Empty errors") {
    var rb = RingBuffer.new()
    val empty_res = rb.pop()
    assert(empty_res is RingError.Empty)

    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 8 {
        rb.push(i * 10)!
        i += 1
    }
    assert(rb.is_full())

    val full_res = rb.push(999)
    assert(full_res is RingError.Full)
    assert(rb.len == 8)
}
```
